ARM: OMAP2: n8x0-maemo: GPIO switches

Maemo's userspace reads the N8x0's switches as Nokia's gpio-switch
driver provided them: /sys/devices/platform/gpio-switch/<name>/ with
state ("open"/"closed", "disconnected"/"connected", "inactive"/
"active"), type and direction. DSME's peripheral module waits on
headphone, slide, cam_act and bat_cover; mce uses slide, kb_lock and
cam_act, multimediad headphone, gpsdriver writes gps_reset and
gps_wakeup.

As Nokia did, the switches come from NOLO's tags (OMAP_TAG_GPIO_SWITCH:
name, GPIO, type, inverted, output), with board-n810.c's debounce times
(200 ms for the slide, lock and headphone; 10 ms otherwise). Inputs
notify state on a change, and, as 2.6.21's sysfs_poll() did, poll
reports only changes (kernfs reports files readable at all times,
which a select() for reading would see continuously). Outputs keep
NOLO's level and are set by writing state.

The slide and the headphone jack are also an input device ("N8x0
switches": SW_KEYPAD_SLIDE, SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT) for other userspace.

